@@ -107,12 +118,25 @@ FUNCTION ISqrt{X: Integer): Integer};
 
 FUNCTION Rnd{Min,Max: Integer): Integer};
 { Rnd:
-   Returns a random number between Max and Min inclusive.  If Min>Max then Min 
+   Returns a random number between Max and Min inclusive.  If Min>Max then Min
    is returned. }
 
    BEGIN
+   { PATCH: Max<=Min checked before ForcedRandomValue, not after -- the degenerate-range clamp is
+     real, unconditional Rnd behavior (pristine source: "If Min>Max then Min is returned", and by the
+     same logic Min=Max has only one possible value regardless of what Random would have picked), so a
+     forced test run should see it too. The original ordering (forced check first) let a forced value
+     override this clamp, silently producing an out-of-[Min,Max] result whenever Min=Max coincided
+     with a nonzero ForcedRandomValue -- confirmed via a real divergence between this harness and the
+     C# port's own PascalMath.Rnd+FixedRandom (which always checks the degenerate range first) in
+     NebulaCases.PatchesMultipleRng2 (NebulaePatches' own Rnd(1,4-Abs(y-InitY)) hits Min=Max at the
+     patch's vertical extremes). Reordering here, not in the C# side, since this clamp is pristine
+     Rnd's own real behavior -- the forced branch is a test-only patch layered on top of it, not the
+     other way around. }
    IF Max<=Min THEN
       Rnd:=Min
+   ELSE IF ForcedRandomValue>=0 THEN
+      Rnd:=Min+ForcedRandomValue
    ELSE
       Rnd:=Random((Max-Min)+1)+Min;
    END;  { Rnd }
